<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Garamantian Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Garamantes, Garamantian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Garamantian Empire was a state of the Garamantes, a Berber-descended people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, which flourished from around the first millennium BCE to the early centuries CE. It built a network of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/foggara">foggara</a> tunnels to tap fossil <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/groundwater-depletion">groundwater</a> and controlled trans-Saharan trade, and it declined as water levels fell and trade collapsed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire.jpg" alt="Garamantian Empire" width="320" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrein · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_Empire_125.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
